{
  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191746": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology",
      "description": "Department: University of Virginia: College at Wise Provost's Office Location: Wise, VA The University of Virginia’s College at Wise, located in the Appalachian Mountains of Southwest Virginia, invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Psychology in the Department of Social Sciences. We seek a collaborative, student-centered teacher, scholar, and clinician who is committed to preparing undergraduate students for graduate education and careers in psychology. The successful candidate will contribute to the Psychology program through undergraduate teaching, academic advising and mentoring, research and scholarship, and service to the department and College. A distinctive component of the position is the opportunity to provide clinical instruction and supervision to undergraduate students as they develop and apply foundational counseling and clinical skills while delivering services under professional supervision. This is a nine-month appointment that will begin in Fall 2027 and is located on the UVA Wise campus in Wise, Virginia. Minimum Qualifications : A PhD or PsyD in Clinical or Counseling Psychology from an APA-accredited doctoral program. ABD candidates will be considered if their degree is conferred by August 2027. Must either hold an active license to practice psychology in the Commonwealth of Virginia or be eligible for Virginia licensure. A candidate who is not licensed at the time of appointment must obtain Virginia licensure during the first year of employment. Academic and clinical preparation sufficient to provide effective supervision to undergraduate students delivering clinical services and to guide students in meeting applicable ethical, legal, professional, and institutional standards. Ability to teach and supervise students in person at the UVA Wise campus. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and other partners in support of the Psychology program. Demonstrated potential for effective undergraduate teaching in a student-centered liberal arts environment. Preferred Qualifications: A record of effective teaching at the undergraduate level. Experience supervising students, interns, or other trainees who provide clinical or counseling services. Experience teaching courses in clinical or counseling psychology, including one or more of the courses identified in this posting. Experience advising and mentoring undergraduate students who are preparing for graduate education or careers in psychology and related fields. Evidence of an active or developing program of research and scholarship. Experience integrating applied, experiential, or community-based learning into undergraduate education. Key Responsibilities : Maintain a 4-4 teaching load, consisting of four courses during each fall and spring semester. Teaching assignments will be based on program needs and may include Introduction to Psychology, Abnormal Psychology, Counseling Techniques, Theories of Psychotherapy, and other courses within the candidate’s area of expertise. Provide clinical instruction and supervision to undergraduate students and assist with student development. Ensure that services are provided in accordance with applicable ethical, legal, professional, and institutional requirements. Participate in departmental and College service, including committee work, program assessment, recruitment, curriculum development, and activities that contribute to the continued growth of the Psychology program. Support students’ academic and professional development through individualized mentoring, career guidance, and assistance with preparation for graduate study and professional opportunities. Maintain an active program of research and scholarship appropriate to a tenure-track appointment at a public liberal arts college. Maintain the professional licensure, knowledge, and competencies necessary to fulfill the clinical responsibilities of the position. Additional information for candidate review : Summer teaching opportunities and research support may be available based on departmental needs, institutional priorities, and available resources. The College recognizes the professional value of continued clinical engagement. Subject to departmental needs, College policies, and applicable approval requirements, scheduling flexibility may be available for outside clinical practice. The successful candidate will join a collegial department committed to undergraduate teaching, close faculty-student engagement, and the academic and professional development of students. The position offers an opportunity to contribute meaningfully to the continued development of the Psychology program’s clinical training and applied learning experiences. Application Instructions : Applicants should submit the following materials: A cover letter (maximum 2 pages) detailing your interest in the position, relevant academic and clinical experience, and how your qualifications match the key responsibilities of the position. A curriculum vitae. A statement on teaching philosophy (2-3 pages double-spaced) highlighting your desire and potential to teach in a liberal arts college setting, including information on mentoring/advising in an academic or workplace environment and clinical supervision. Contact information for three professional references who can attest to your teaching potential and clinical skills and qualifications. The review of applications will begin on November 1 and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration please submit application materials by October 31, 2026. Additional Requirements: Background checks will be conducted on all new hires prior to employment. Location: This position is based in Wise, Virginia, situated in the far southwestern corner of the state near the Kentucky and Tennessee borders. Anticipated Salary: $70,000 - $76,000 Contact: Questions regarding this position should be directed to Hannah Addington, Human Resources Recruiting Specialist @ hrc2j@uvawise.edu UVA Wise is an equal opportunity employer committed to excellence, affordable access, and unwavering support of a collaborative and diverse community.  Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Employee fulfills duties as a “responsible employee” under Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972. A Responsible employee includes any employee: who has the authority to take action to redress sexual violence; who has been given the duty of reporting incidents of sexual violence or any other misconduct by students to the Title IX Coordinator or other appropriate school designee; or whom a student could reasonably believe has this authority or duty. UVA Wise is committed to helping the campus community provide for their own safety and security. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report containing information on campus security and personal safety, including alerts, fire safety, crime prevention tips, and crime statistics is available at www.uvawise.edu/ASR . A copy is available upon request by calling 276-328-0190 or 276-376-3451."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195265": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Education",
      "description": "Department: University of Virginia: College at Wise Provost's Office Location: Wise, VA The University of Virginia's College at Wise, a nationally ranked public liberal arts institution nestled in the mountains of southwestern Virginia, seeks applications for a tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor of Education position beginning January 2027. This is a full-time, 9-month appointment. About the Department: The UVA Wise Education Department fosters a collaborative and supportive environment where faculty work closely together on accreditation, curriculum planning, clinical faculty training, advising, and other initiatives. Primary Responsibilities · Teach 12 credits per semester across undergraduate and graduate courses in both in-person and virtual modalities · Supervise student teaching internships · Participate in program development, review, and management · Maintain an active research and publication agenda · Build and maintain relationships with local educators and school administrators · Advise and recruit students · Contribute to departmental and college-wide service activities Teaching Areas Potentially Include (general education, undergraduate and graduate) · Foundations of Education · Classroom Management and Behaviors · Assessment for Student and Teacher Growth · Foundations of Assessment · Educational Technology Required Qualifications · PhD/EdD in Education or related field (completion by December 2026 acceptable) · Minimum three years of PK-12 teaching experience · Demonstrated teaching excellence · Expertise in curriculum and instruction development · Strong organizational and interpersonal skills · Commitment to innovative teaching approaches · Excellent written and oral communication abilities Preferred Qualifications · Terminal degree in Curriculum & Instruction or similar focus · Experience with diverse student populations · Knowledge of current education laws, policies, and regulations · Experiential knowledge of accreditation policies and procedures · Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in an academic setting Additional Requirements · Technological proficiency and online course delivery · Comprehensive focus for academic and community service and mentorship · Ability to meet deadlines and work independently · Strong presentation and group facilitation skills · Experience managing sensitive situations with discretion Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Successful candidates will be required to demonstrate teaching competence through a teaching demonstration during the interview process. Additional Requirements Background checks will be conducted on all new hires prior to employment. Required Documents Cover Letter, CV/Resume, and References Location This position is based in Wise, Virginia, situated in the far southwestern corner of the state near the Kentucky and Tennessee borders. Anticipated Salary: $65,000 $75,000; depending on qualifications and experience. Contact Questions regarding this position should be directed to Hannah Addington, Human Resources Recruiting Specialist @ hrc2j@uvawise.edu UVA Wise is an equal opportunity employer committed to excellence, affordable access, and unwavering support of a collaborative and diverse community.  Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Employee fulfills duties as a “responsible employee” under Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972. A Responsible employee includes any employee: who has the authority to take action to redress sexual violence; who has been given the duty of reporting incidents of sexual violence or any other misconduct by students to the Title IX Coordinator or other appropriate school designee; or whom a student could reasonably believe has this authority or duty. UVA Wise is committed to helping the campus community provide for their own safety and security. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report containing information on campus security and personal safety, including alerts, fire safety, crime prevention tips, and crime statistics is available at www.uvawise.edu/ASR . A copy is available upon request by calling 276-328-0190 or 276-376-3451."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/196586": {
      "title": "Instructor or Assistant Professor of Business",
      "description": "Department: University of Virginia: College at Wise Provost's Office Location: Wise, VA Posted: Oct 29, 2026 The University of Virginia’s College at Wise, a division of the University of Virginia located in Wise, Virginia, invites applications for a full-time, nine-month, tenure-track faculty position in the Department of Business and Economics beginning August 2027. Appointment will be at the rank of Instructor or Assistant Professor, depending on the successful candidate’s academic credentials and qualifications. The department seeks a versatile faculty member whose primary teaching specialization is in one of the following areas: ·         Finance ·         Economics ·         Analytics ·         Accounting Applicants must identify a primary teaching area from the four areas listed above and a secondary teaching area in any subject taught by the Department of Business and Economics in their Cover Letter. The secondary area will be another one of the four primary areas or another subject area within the Department's curriculum. Candidates are not expected to teach across all four primary areas. The successful candidate will contribute substantively in both the primary and secondary areas according to departmental needs and documented qualifications. About the Department The Department of Business and Economics emphasizes teaching excellence, student mentoring, and applied learning within a public liberal arts setting. The department offers undergraduate programs across business, economics, and hospitality and graduate study in Technology Management and Data Analytics, creating opportunities for interdisciplinary teaching and professional engagement. Responsibilities Develop and teach introductory and advanced undergraduate courses in the candidate’s primary and secondary teaching areas, and graduate courses when appropriately qualified and assigned. Instruction may include face-to-face and online formats. Advise and mentor students; support recruitment, retention, and professional development; and maintain regular office hours. Contribute to curriculum development, assessment, departmental committees, and College service. Engage in scholarly and professional activity appropriate to the rank and appointment. Collaborate with business, industry, and community partners to support applied learning, internships, and other experiential opportunities. Minimum Qualifications Instructor: An earned master’s degree by the start date in Finance, Economics, Analytics, Accounting, Business Administration, or a closely related field. Assistant Professor: An earned Ph.D., or equivalent terminal degree by the start date in Finance, Economics, Analytics, Accounting, Business Administration, or a closely related field. Advanced ABD candidates will be considered provided the terminal degree is completed by the start date. All candidates : Academic preparation and/or relevant professional qualifications sufficient to teach in one primary area from Finance, Economics, Analytics, or Accounting and in at least one additional subject area taught by the Department of Business and Economics; excellent oral and written communication skills; demonstrated commitment to student-centered teaching and mentoring; ability to collaborate with colleagues; and ability to teach in the assigned instructional formats. Qualifications in both teaching areas must be documented in the application materials and satisfy the College's faculty-credentialing requirements. Location: This position is based in Wise, Virginia, situated in the far southwestern corner of the state near the Kentucky and Tennessee borders. This position requires regular on-campus participation in teaching, advising, office hours, and departmental and College activities. Online teaching assignments do not make this a fully remote appointment. Anticipated nine-month salary range: Instructor: $68,000-$80,000. Assistant Professor: $85,000-$125,000. Final compensation will reflect the successful candidate's qualifications, teaching areas and experience within the applicable approved range. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, with full consideration given to applications received by December 22, 2026. The position will remain open until filled. Required Documents Cover Letter, CV/Resume, Statement of Teaching Philosophy, unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required upon hiring), and contact information for three references. Candidates seeking consideration at the Assistant Professor rank should also submit a statement of research interests and evidence of scholarly activity or research potential. The cover letter must identify the rank sought, a primary teaching area from Finance, Economics, Analytics, or Accounting, and a secondary teaching area from among subjects taught by the Department of Business and Economics. Application materials must document preparation to teach in both areas. Reference letters are not required with the initial application; applicants will be notified before references are contacted. Contact Questions regarding this position should be directed to Hannah Addington, Human Resources Recruiting Specialist @ hrc2j@uvawise.edu UVA Wise is an equal opportunity employer committed to excellence, affordable access, and unwavering support of a collaborative and diverse community.  Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Employee fulfills duties as a “responsible employee” under Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972.  A Responsible employee includes any employee:  who has the authority to take action to redress sexual violence; who has been given the duty of reporting incidents of sexual violence or any other misconduct by students to the Title IX Coordinator or other appropriate school designee; or whom a student could reasonably believe has this authority or duty. UVA Wise is committed to helping the campus community provide for their own safety and security.  The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report containing information on campus security and personal safety, including alerts, fire safety, crime prevention tips, and crime statistics is available at www.uvawise.edu/ASR .  A copy is available upon request by calling 276-328-0190 or 276-376-3451."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/196587": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Nursing",
      "description": "Department: University of Virginia: College at Wise Provost's Office Location: Wise, VA Posted: Oct 29, 2026 The University of Virginia’s College at Wise, a division of the University of Virginia, invites applications for a Prelicensure Instructor in Nursing. The University of Virginia’s College at Wise is a nationally ranked four-year undergraduate public liberal arts college located in the mountains of southwestern Virginia. The successful candidate must have a minimum of a master’s degree in nursing or relevant profession with bedside experience in Mental Health, Obstetrics, and/or Pediatrics clinical practice.  Experience in teaching in a Prelicensure BSN Nursing Program.  The college seeks a candidate that can be hired at the Assistant or Associate Professor level.  Appointment to an instruction position. Candidates with a PhD or DNP degree will be at a Professorate level commensurate with experience. Additional Requirements: Background checks will be conducted on all new hires prior to employment. Required Documents: Cover Letter, CV/Resume, Unofficial Transcripts (Official transcripts required upon hiring), and Three References Location: This position is based in Wise, Virginia, situated in the far southwestern corner of the state near the Kentucky and Tennessee borders. Anticipated Salary : $60,000 - $70,000 Contact: Questions regarding this position should be directed to Hannah Addington, Human Resources Recruiting Specialist @ hrc2j@uvawise.edu UVA Wise is an equal opportunity employer committed to excellence, affordable access, and unwavering support of a collaborative and diverse community.  Women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Employee fulfills duties as a “responsible employee” under Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972.  A Responsible employee includes any employee:  who has the authority to take action to redress sexual violence; who has been given the duty of reporting incidents of sexual violence or any other misconduct by students to the Title IX Coordinator or other appropriate school designee; or whom a student could reasonably believe has this authority or duty. UVA Wise is committed to helping the campus community provide for their own safety and security.  The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report containing information on campus security and personal safety, including alerts, fire safety, crime prevention tips, and crime statistics is available at www.uvawise.edu/ASR .  A copy is available upon request by calling 276-328-0190 or 276"
